      "message": "the intended population is everyone.  there might be an argument to not modifying behavior on existing devices, so it\u0027d be an opt-out situation, not an opt-in.\n\nbut i\u0027m not seeing a situation where this would make correctly working code break.  it might make broken code that would have triggered a crash no longer crash, but at that point arguably it\u0027s already a bug, and how it manifests or is detected isn\u0027t exactly guaranteed since it\u0027s a bug.",
